{
  "meta": {
    "source": "Computed by npm run build:data from data/troubleshooting.json (shower mix temperature), data/fixture-flow-rates.json (shower flow), data/site.json (tank setting) and data/computed/inlet-temps.json with assets/js/formulas.js",
    "sourceUrl": "https://hotwatermath.com/methodology/",
    "sourceDate": "2026-11-12",
    "notes": "Hot share = (shower temperature − inlet) ÷ (tank setting − inlet), formulas.hotShareOfMix; hot gallons = flow × minutes × hot share, formulas.hotGallonsDrawn. Reheat time per gallon scales with the temperature rise (formulas.temperatureRise), so winter ÷ summer rise − 1 is how much longer each gallon takes. No heat loss in the pipes is counted, so real draws are a little higher. The shower length is our example."
  },
